{"type":"message","id":"6afcdc94","parentId":"d86d5b9d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T02:22:24.735Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTTP 500 error. The send endpoint is returning a 500 with \"error code: 1101\". This is a server-side error. The worker's send handler is failing internally. The `/send` endpoint seems to have a bug or the worker's handler is crashing.\n\nBut the `/history` endpoint works fine. Let me check if maybe the API key is correct by checking the headers - wait, history also works with this API key, so the key is fine.\n\nThe issue is that the POST `/send` endpoint is returning a 500 error. This is a bug in the platform's worker code itself.\n\nLet me try different formats - maybe it expects `channel` and `message` instead of `threadId` and `content`:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-90ea209e-00d8-4774-bbc0-f4856b84d11b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"channel\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"test\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2215,"output":242,"cacheRead":18256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20713,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779243733938,"responseId":"chatcmpl-056162ac-3ec0-4c03-989a-0a92ccfd9b6b"}}
