{"type":"message","id":"e806afc1","parentId":"8fd8871b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T02:22:48.931Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still the same error. The 500 from /send suggests the endpoint is broken or the worker has a bug. Since history works and the GET on /send works, the worker itself is up but the POST handler is crashing.\n\nLet me try with `thread` instead of `threadId`, and also let me try without content type header.\n\nActually, let me think about what else might be going on. Maybe the API expects a different JSON structure. Let me check what the 500 response body is more carefully - it says \"error code: 1101\" in the body. This is likely a custom error message.\n\nMaybe it requires `type` field or `echoAsset`. \n\nLooking at the history endpoint's response format, I can see the message structure includes fields like `replyTo` and `echoAsset`. Let me try reconstructing the full message structure with those fields to see if that resolves the 500 error.\n\nActually, the HTTP 500 response body is just \"error code: 1101\" - a custom error payload rather than a standard Workers error, which means the route is definitely registered and returning something. But if the POST handler itself is crashing internally, no amount of field tweaking will help since it can't even parse the request. Let me try simplifying to just a plain text or form-encoded payload instead of JSON.\n\nI should document what I found in the status report rather than continuing to debug this.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2978fb22-1439-4c1a-80dc-fd083380d2c7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat_02:15'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minim